{"id":31,"date":"2011-09-13T14:12:23","date_gmt":"2011-09-13T14:12:23","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.wordpress.com\/?p=31"},"modified":"2021-01-06T12:21:58","modified_gmt":"2021-01-06T12:21:58","slug":"processing","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/processing\/","title":{"rendered":"Processing"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/5.jpg\"><img data-attachment-id=\"32\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/5\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/5.jpg?fit=718%2C295&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"718,295\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"5\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/5.jpg?fit=300%2C123&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/5.jpg?fit=605%2C249&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"aligncenter size-medium wp-image-32\" title=\"5\" alt=\"space echo\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/5.jpg?w=300&#038;resize=300%2C123\" width=\"300\" height=\"123\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/5.jpg?w=718&amp;ssl=1 718w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/5.jpg?resize=300%2C123&amp;ssl=1 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>The total signal latency, in+out, in the signal-flow is at around 8ms. This presents a challenge regarding timing and I had to choose the effects I use based some what on this.<\/p>\n<p>I did a quick run-through of available effects in Ableton Live and Max for Live and checked how the sounded on the drum set with the setup I explained earlier. After going through all of them, also their presets, I was left with around 20 that I really liked. Probably because they made a statement, affecting the sound with hard processing, so that the outcome was quite untraditional.<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>After a while playing with the effects, I noticed that I was only using a few of them:<\/p>\n<p>1 &#8211; a delay which is so fast that it generate complex tones.<br \/>\n2 &#8211; a delay that makes a fixed amount of repetitions at the same volume, also called \u201cdrrrr\u201d.<br \/>\n3 &#8211; a ping-pong delay fixed to play 4 against 3, synced to the sequencers global timing.<br \/>\n4 &#8211; a reverb<br \/>\n5 &#8211; a beat repeater<br \/>\n6 &#8211; a grain delay<br \/>\n7 &#8211; an auto filter<br \/>\n8 &#8211; another reverb<\/p>\n<p>In addition to this I have four loopers and some mechanisms to trigger samples by hitting the drums.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The total signal latency, in+out, in the signal-flow is at around 8ms. This presents a challenge regarding timing and I had to choose the effects I use based some what on this. I did a quick run-through of available effects &hellip;<\/p>\n<p class=\"read-more\"> <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/processing\/\"> <span class=\"screen-reader-text\">Processing<\/span> Read More &raquo;<\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":32,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"jetpack